# Copy to deploy/fleet/env/live.env (chmod 600). Live credentials stay here.
# Live resolves the `live` credential slot, not the default slot Paper uses
# (app/broker/alpaca/profile/credentials.py:59-66) — confirmed against the
# running Live lane's own environment (variable names only, never a value).
# Strictly it is the configuration profile that names the slot, not the mode:
# "Live uses the `live` slot" is this deployment's convention, not something
# the code forces.
# This file previously named the default-slot pair below, byte-identical to
# paper.env.example; an operator who copied it got two empty variables and,
# per docs/runbooks/add-an-alpaca-account.md §6, an unauthenticated request
# against the real-money endpoint with nothing surfacing an error. See #2156.
FLEET_CLERK_ID=
FLEET_WORKER_KEY=
FLEET_AGENT_SERVICE_TOKEN=
FLEET_COORDINATOR_SERVICE_TOKEN=
ALPACA_CREDENTIAL_LIVE_KEY_ID=
ALPACA_CREDENTIAL_LIVE_SECRET_KEY=
# The retained market-data session is read-only and this client id must
# differ from Paper's value in paper.env. Documentary only: compose.fleet.dev.yaml
# sets IBKR_CLIENT_ID under `environment:`, which always wins over this
# env_file value for the same key (Compose's own rule; the whole reason the
# four keys above are env_file-only there). 1 is the value the running
# override currently deploys with — authoritative for this PR, which
# transcribes what runs, not what was originally planned. To use a different
# id, set FLEET_LIVE_IBKR_CLIENT_ID (not this line).
IBKR_CLIENT_ID=1
